WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.782
Welcome to UFI Career Studio. Handle an offer

00:00:03.782 --> 00:00:07.564
conversation. Review the full package, prepare a specific

00:00:07.564 --> 00:00:11.346
request, and give yourself time to make a

00:00:11.346 --> 00:00:15.128
clear decision. We will work through five practical

00:00:15.128 --> 00:00:18.911
steps, with examples you can adapt to your

00:00:18.911 --> 00:00:19.856
own experience.

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:24.560
Review the complete package instead of focusing only

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.453
on salary. Consider the work itself, benefits, time

00:00:28.453 --> 00:00:32.346
off, schedule, location, and opportunities to learn. Ask

00:00:32.346 --> 00:00:36.239
how any bonus or equity component works rather

00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:40.132
than treating it as guaranteed cash. Write down

00:00:40.132 --> 00:00:44.025
anything you do not understand. The right comparison

00:00:44.025 --> 00:00:47.918
is between the full terms and your priorities,

00:00:47.918 --> 00:00:50.351
not just the largest number.

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:54.646
Prepare a reasonable request using the scope of

00:00:54.646 --> 00:00:58.125
the job, your relevant experience, and current information

00:00:58.125 --> 00:01:01.605
about comparable roles. Check the location and level

00:01:01.605 --> 00:01:05.084
when comparing figures. Decide which terms matter most

00:01:05.084 --> 00:01:08.563
to you and where you have flexibility. This

00:01:08.563 --> 00:01:12.042
is a preparation exercise, not a guarantee that

00:01:12.042 --> 00:01:15.522
the employer can change the offer or that

00:01:15.522 --> 00:01:17.696
a particular number is appropriate.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.737
Express genuine interest, then make a clear and

00:01:21.737 --> 00:01:24.975
specific request. You could say that you are

00:01:24.975 --> 00:01:28.212
excited about the responsibilities and would like to

00:01:28.212 --> 00:01:31.449
discuss an adjustment based on the role scope

00:01:31.449 --> 00:01:34.686
and your experience. Keep the explanation concise and

00:01:34.686 --> 00:01:37.924
factual. Avoid inventing another offer or making a

00:01:37.924 --> 00:01:41.161
threat you do not intend to follow through

00:01:41.161 --> 00:01:41.566
on.

00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:45.768
After making your request, pause and listen. The

00:01:45.768 --> 00:01:49.119
person may need approval or may explain a

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:52.471
constraint. Ask what flexibility is available and consider

00:01:52.471 --> 00:01:55.822
whether another term would address your priorities. You

00:01:55.822 --> 00:01:59.173
do not have to accept immediately during the

00:01:59.173 --> 00:02:02.525
call. Confirm the decision deadline and ask for

00:02:02.525 --> 00:02:05.457
time to review if you need it.

00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:10.039
Ask for the final terms in writing and

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:13.744
check that they match the conversation. Review the

00:02:13.744 --> 00:02:17.449
responsibilities, compensation, start date, and any conditions before

00:02:17.449 --> 00:02:21.154
deciding. If a term is unclear or has

00:02:21.154 --> 00:02:24.860
legal or financial consequences, seek appropriate professional advice.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:28.565
Your practice task is to list your three

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:32.270
priorities and draft a short, respectful request you

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.123
could comfortably say aloud.
